  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Program Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the initial architecture and file structure for the program. I\'ve started by outlining the essential data types, specifically the `ProgramItem` type, which will encapsulate key information such as ID, title, type, description, and various attributes related to the program\'s purpose and audience. The design includes optional properties like `imageUrl` and `tallyUrl`, and a flag `isBuilt`. I will continue to think about this file, as well as new files.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Structures**\n\nNow, I\'m fleshing out the specific data structures. I\'ve defined `OrderType`, `OrderDefinition`, `GeneratedContent`, and `ChatMessage` to represent the relationships between program content, orders, and interactions. The `ChatMessage` will capture the user and assistant\'s exchanges, including the `orderTriggered`. I am also working on the data structure for the `/src/data/defaultPrograms.ts` file, and I\'ve started building the 8 default workshops and programs, complete with pain points, values, and image URLs.\n\n\n**Analyzing Program Integration**\n\nI\'m now incorporating specific workshops and content types (`LIFE ACTION`, `S\341\273\250C B\341\273\200N`, and `SINH VI\303\212N`) into the program, adding high-performing comment templates from TikTok, LinkedIn, and Facebook. I\'ve begun defining the server endpoints, including `/api/health` and `/api/extract-program` which utilizes Gemini to analyze various inputs and return a clean `ProgramItem` with structured data. There\'s also `/api/generate-order` with strict prompt rules for Facebook.\n\n\n**Defining Marketing Strategies**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the marketing strategies for the program. I\'ve broken down each platform\'s approach: TikTok emphasizes empathy and offers; Threads leans towards candid storytelling and DM engagement; LinkedIn adopts an HR/L&D-focused, data-driven approach with a 1:1 consultation; and Email provides relatable hooks with insightful questions. A new `/api/chat` endpoint enables interactive assistance, immediately returning order menus upon \"Hi\" and parsing natural commands.\n\n\n**Designing Frontend Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the frontend components within `/src/components/`. Key pieces include `Header.tsx`, `OrderDashboard.tsx`, and a deep generation studio in `OrderGeneratorModal.tsx` and `GeneratorWorkspace.tsx`. I\'ve outlined a rich `GeneratedResultCard.tsx` with one-click copy and a direct DM follow-up script generator. The program management functionalities are in `ProgramManager.tsx` and an interactive chat assistant is built in `AIChatAssistant.tsx`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 459269291
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
