    thinking: "**Designing Frontend Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on crafting the frontend. My priority is a modular, clean, responsive, and intuitive user interface. I\'ve started with `src/components/Navbar.tsx`, planning to include a prominent logo or app title, \"ORDER AI SI\303\212U NH\303\200N,\" alongside a subtitle. I\'m also considering a quick prompt to guide new users, maybe something like \"G\303\265 \'Hi\' m\341\273\237.\"\n\n\n**Defining Order Menu Structure**\n\nI\'m now structuring the main order menu. The plan includes a prominent \"Order\" button for initiating chat or order actions. I\'m structuring this into tabs for different functionalities: a direct generator and workbench, workshop/program management, an automated chat assistant, and benchmark templates. A quick stats badge will display active workshops/programs and a compliance check.\n\n\n**Refining Workshop Outputs**\n\nI\'m now refining the workshop outputs, specifically the \"\360\237\232\200 AI T\341\272\241o Content & K\341\273\213ch B\341\272\243n DM\" button. I\'ve built in a loading state. I\'m focusing on providing multiple high-converting variations, one-click copy functionality, character count, and explanations. I\'m also developing a DM follow-up script with empathy, qualifying questions, and a warm invite.\n\n\n**Developing Workshop Inputs**\n\nI\'m now focusing on workshop and program input methods. I\'m building a modal for adding new workshops/programs, incorporating AI-driven automated extraction from various sources. I\'m exploring options for inputting data, including Tally/Google Form links, text descriptions, and even poster images. I\'m implementing a preview and local storage functionality. I\'m also ensuring edit, delete, and type-switching capabilities, along with active/inactive toggles. I\'m prioritizing user-friendly input for seamless creation.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Integrating Interactive AI Chat**\n\nI\'m integrating an interactive terminal within `AIChatModal.tsx` and `AIChatDrawer.tsx`. The interface will be preloaded with a greeting and prompt. The plan is for the user to type \"Hi\" to trigger the automated 7-order menu. Users can also enter a command like \"Order 1 [m\303\264 t\341\272\243 clip]\" which instantly generates a result displayed in chat. I\'m also creating a function to test DM responses.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 91165433
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
